er than before  i know that for example my mini story is  for turkish and the same is true for  persian and arabic  when i started it was just noise i  couldn't figure out what they were  saying what words meant and how they fit  it together and now i would say  at least 50 of the 60 stories i  understand them perfectly so i have  achieved something even if i struggle to  use these words and even if i make  mistakes and i make the same mistakes  over and over again it's difficult to  nail the tenses in turkish and but i  know also that in time it'll get better  if i just you know continue doing what  i'm doing so it's enjoyable to me the  other thing about language learning is  for me  first of all i'm retired so there is no  limit  to how much i can improve in any  language or how many new languages i can  discover it's essentially limitless  so i my whole retirement is full  whatever else i have going if there's a  slow  moment i can go back to learning  languages and  learning languages the way i do  heavily reliant on  listening here  it makes household tasks  enjoyable cleaning up  uh cleaning up in the garage working out  there's so many such in the car i can  always listen  of course listening is not enough  uh listening is a big part of sort  of ingraining the phrases phrases and  words into your  into your brain in a way that you'll be  able to use them  but reading is also key in order to  expand your vocabulary so i do i do  combine both of them but the listing is  so easy to organize  and it makes the everyday tasks um  enjoyable i don't mind cleaning up i'm  going to listen to  whatever turkish and it's enjoyable  when i understand it so much better than  i used to understand it so those are my  sense  or call them milestones of achievement  so  i enjoy languages because of the  discovery i enjoy languages because i  know that it's an activity that is an  activity an exercise in discovery but  also it leads you to these other things  friends that i'll b